# Phase 8e: a small hand-authored cube -- the physics demo's own falling
# object (see engine::RigidBody/Collider, include/engine/physics.hpp, and
# assets/scenes/default.json's own "falling_cube" entity). A cube, not a
# reuse of scene.obj's own table/box/pyramid, so it reads as one distinct
# "thing being dropped" rather than a fourth piece of that static furniture
# set.
#
# Centered on its own local origin -- every vertex at +/-0.25 on every axis
# -- so this mesh's own local bounding box exactly matches Collider's
# halfExtent (0.25, the same value assets/scenes/default.json's "collider"
# block gives this entity): the entity's Transform position IS the physics
# center this file's local (0,0,0) sits at, with no separate mesh-to-collider
# offset for stepPhysics() (physics.cpp) to account for.
#
# Same shared-texcoord/face-normal box layout as scene.obj's own Table/
# BoxOnTable objects (see that file's header comment) -- 4 vt entries
# (bottom-left, bottom-right, top-right, top-left) and 6 vn face normals --
# reused verbatim rather than re-derived, since this is the exact same
# "axis-aligned box" shape those two objects already are.

mtllib falling_cube.mtl

# --- Shared texcoords (bottom-left, bottom-right, top-right, top-left) ---
vt 0.0 0.0
vt 1.0 0.0
vt 1.0 1.0
vt 0.0 1.0

# --- Shared face normals (box faces) ---
vn 0.0 0.0 1.0
vn 0.0 0.0 -1.0
vn 1.0 0.0 0.0
vn -1.0 0.0 0.0
vn 0.0 1.0 0.0
vn 0.0 -1.0 0.0

# --- Cube: half-extent 0.25, centered on the local origin -> x/y/z each in
# [-0.25, 0.25].
v -0.25 -0.25 -0.25
v  0.25 -0.25 -0.25
v  0.25 -0.25  0.25
v -0.25 -0.25  0.25
v -0.25  0.25 -0.25
v  0.25  0.25 -0.25
v  0.25  0.25  0.25
v -0.25  0.25  0.25

o FallingCube
usemtl FallingCube
f 4/1/1 3/2/1 7/3/1 8/4/1
f 2/1/2 1/2/2 5/3/2 6/4/2
f 3/1/3 2/2/3 6/3/3 7/4/3
f 1/1/4 4/2/4 8/3/4 5/4/4
f 8/1/5 7/2/5 6/3/5 5/4/5
f 1/1/6 2/2/6 3/3/6 4/4/6
